In RAN #76 meeting, a Study Item on evaluation methodology of new V2X use cases for LTE and NR was agreed [1]. The objective of the SI is “to establish the evaluation methodology to be used in evaluating technical solutions to support the full set of 5G V2X use cases as identified in TR 22.886 and the full set of 5G RAN requirements in TR38.913.” In an offline email discussion on the RAN1 reflector [2] companies raised multiple issues to be addressed to meet the objective of the SI and included proposed solutions. The email discussion resulted in an agreed list of open issues related to the evaluation methodology [3] and companies were requested to provide their views on how to address this list of open issues. A follow-up email discussion, after the RAN1#90bis meeting, marked as “[90b-NR-02]” resulted in agreements on a list of evaluation criteria and a few cases that require further study. Contribution [9] submitted to the 3GPP RAN 1 #90bis meeting, discusses the so-called “obstructed LOS” for the V2V channel modeling. This contribution discusses some aspects related to sidelink channel modeling. The discussion below deals with carrier frequencies below 6GHz; however, the statements below and the proposals are applicable for channel both below and above 6GHz and the technical input of this contribution should be considered in the SI. This contribution is a revision of contribution ‎[21].

